  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Acts as a coreceptor with members of the frizzled family of seven-transmembrane spanning receptors to transduce signal by Wnt proteins. Upon Wnt binding, LRP5 is phosphorylated at conserved PPPSP motifs by GSK3 and CK1, creating docking sites for Axin. This sequesters Axin away from the beta-catenin destruction complex, leading to beta-catenin stabilization and activation of TCF/LEF-dependent transcription. Critical regulator of bone mass through control of osteoblast proliferation and differentiation.",
    "catalytic_activity": null,
    "subcellular_location": [
      "Plasma membrane",
      "Endoplasmic reticulum",
      "Cytoplasm"
    ],
    "tissue_specificity": "Widely expressed with highest levels in liver and aorta. Expressed in osteoblasts lining endosteal and trabecular bone surfaces. Also detected in bile duct epithelium and various other tissues.",
