    "pathway_role_summary": "LRP5 is a critical coreceptor in canonical Wnt signaling. Upon Wnt binding, LRP5 associates with Frizzled receptors and becomes phosphorylated at PPPSP motifs, creating docking sites for Axin. This sequesters the destruction complex components from beta-catenin, leading to beta-catenin stabilization and nuclear translocation. LRP5 is particularly important in bone development and homeostasis, where it regulates osteoblast proliferation and differentiation."
  },
