    "data_quality_notes": "Comprehensive data available. LRP5 is closely related to LRP6 (73% sequence identity), and many studies characterize both receptors together. Some structural and kinetic data are from LRP6 studies but apply to LRP5. Exact amino acid sequence may vary slightly between databases. PPPSP motif positions are approximate and require experimental validation. No high-resolution experimental structure available specifically for LRP5; crystal structures primarily from LRP6 or LRP5/6 chimeras. Kinetic parameters for GSK3-mediated phosphorylation are derived from studies on the Axin-GSK3-beta-catenin system.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "LRP5 is essential for canonical Wnt pathway modeling as the primary coreceptor that determines pathway activation state. Five PPPSP phosphorylation sites create redundant Axin binding sites with cooperative effects. Antagonist binding (DKK1, Sclerostin) provides regulatory control points. LRP5-specific mutations cause dramatic bone phenotypes, highlighting importance in tissue-specific signaling. Key for modeling: (1) ternary complex formation with Wnt and Frizzled, (2) sequential phosphorylation creating graded Axin recruitment, (3) competition between activators (Wnt) and antagonists (DKK1/SOST), (4) receptor endocytosis via Kremen-DKK complex."
  }
